{"total_count":10,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166","id":6267763537,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZZ7UQ","number":1166,"title":"Reconcile duplicate NBRC1257 and NBRC1321 stock proposals before integration","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-08T04:56:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T05:17:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The frozen Worker 1 shard proposes four new owners for two equivalent preparations. This concerns unpublished proposals; no maintained owners have been merged or changed.\n\n| Preparation | Proposals | Primary evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| CO2-saturated bicarbonate | `NSC-PROP-NBRC_1257_Bicarbonate_Solution` and `CS-PROP-NBRC1321_CO2_BICARBONATE_STOCK` | Both sources specify 8.4 g NaHCO3 plus 100 mL distilled water, CO2 saturation, sealed CO2 bottles and autoclaving. |\n| Sulfide from nonahydrate | `NSC-PROP-NBRC_1257_Sulfide_Solution` and `CS-PROP-NBRC1321_SULFIDE_STOCK` | NBRC1257 uses 12 g Na2S·9H2O plus 50 mL water; NBRC1321 uses 24 g plus 100 mL. Both are nominally 1 M, filter sterilized and stored under N2. The batch scales differ by two; the evidence does not establish distinct preparations. |\n\nPrimary pages: [NBRC1257](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1257) and [NBRC1321](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1321). Exact captures and payloads are bound in the finding below.\n\nReconcile each pair to one proposed owner while preserving both source cases, every occurrence, raw labels, original batch scales and receiving-medium amounts. Source numbers alone do not define distinct substances. This does not establish equivalence with generic 84 g/L bicarbonate, neutralized sulfide or 5% sulfide. Preserve added-water amounts without asserting measured final volume; keep generic source-local labels non-resolving. The author/coordinator must select the retained proposal; this issue selects no identifier and authorizes no maintained-owner merge.\n\nThe same-source phenanthrene and Metal44 pairs were already reported by the worker and remain separate reconciliation items. Current open-issue deduplication found no tracker for these two cross-source pairs; #1163 concerns the earlier stock-completeness gap.\n\nEvidence under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w01-shard-coordinator-review-v2/`: `finding-003-duplicate-preparations.json`, SHA256 `8395d68231535cb509d7fef4b1d1ad3405498c50fc71d9e9ce259c5219749261`; peer `duplicate-addendum-v1/comparison.json`, SHA256 `1efe59deafe86709301536500ac9a885ab9b2d793144591c1b3ab8c92a573a26`. Frozen proposal manifest SHA256 `eb456ecef3f68b587a2f0281336f88b33679eb8d65a38f842661457ec05866f0`.\n\nRequire native validation and independent re-review of the reconciled final payloads. No role, component, mapping-release or whole-record approval follows from this issue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1166/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163","id":6267639045,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZSVBQ","number":1163,"title":"Complete worker01 source-defined stock proposals or document specific blockers","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-08T04:38:13Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T05:17:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Worker01: complete source-defined stocks need bounded proposals or explicit blockers\n\nThe provisional 188-case shard contains nine decisions (seven source-qualified preparations) with recovered primary formulations, `proposal_ids: []`, and `missing_requirement: null`. They share a generic future-integration deferral. Preserving stocks separately from dry solutes is correct; it does not explain why a source-qualified proposal cannot be prepared.\n\nThis finding is bounded to the frozen decisions below, not all stock cases or a final-head approval. No source, mapping, role, or release change is approved by this issue.\n\n| Case index | Source label | Verified source scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| 17 | CaCl2 solution (0.1 M)*** | [CS-P-NBRC-1339](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1339): 0.1 M CaCl2 aqueous stock; distilled water and autoclaving are explicit. |\n| 92 | CaCl2 solution | [CS-P-NBRC-1339](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1339): The short label is locally resolved to that 0.1 M stock in M9-Phenanthrene, without global synonym promotion. |\n| 101 | MgSO4 solution (1 M)*** | [CS-P-NBRC-1339](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1339): 1 M MgSO4 aqueous stock; distilled water and autoclaving are explicit; no dry hydrate identity is inferred. |\n| 66 | MgSO4 solution | [CS-P-NBRC-1339](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1339): The short label is locally resolved to that 1 M stock in M9-Phenanthrene, without global synonym promotion. |\n| 68 | Phenanthrene solution (250 mM) in dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO)**** | [CS-P-NBRC-1339](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1339): 250 mM phenanthrene in DMSO, filtered with DMSO-safe filters; solvent is explicitly supplied. |\n| 116 | Tween 80 solution** | [CS-P-NBRC-881](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=881): Preparation lists Tween 80 50 g and distilled water 1 L; preserve added-water amount rather than assume measured final volume. |\n| 107 | Bicarbonate solution (1.0 M)*** | [CS-P-NBRC-1321](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1321): NaHCO3 8.4 g and distilled water 100 mL; CO2 saturation, sealed CO2 atmosphere and autoclaving are explicit. Existing 84 g/L overlap requires bounded ownership resolution. |\n| 114 | Sulfide solution (1.0 M)******* | [CS-P-NBRC-1321](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1321): Na2S·9H2O 24 g and distilled water 100 mL; filtration and N2 storage are explicit. |\n| 128 | FeCl3 solution | [CS-P-JCM-1036](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1036): FeCl3·6H2O 0.15 g and distilled water 300 mL, freshly prepared; source-qualified nested Solution B occurrences only. |\n\nRequired resolution: prepare source-qualified native proposals or document a concrete remaining scientific/ownership blocker for each case. Bind the long/short CaCl2 and MgSO4 labels only to their exact source occurrences. Resolve existing-owner/cross-worker overlap before integration. Preserve added-water amounts rather than assume final volume; do not guess hydration, merge stocks by their solute, or approve roles. Require native validation and independent review before publication.\n\nFrozen decisions SHA-256: `5dbbf63b1736fbac74bc5f6457be48fb3613b3bd38a3ab4d4e37a279ce3ce704`. Frozen proposals SHA-256: `eb27d6de8b6a3403b131cb9ec1e21c65d300a2a977fa2acabdf6b463dcda1354`. Full case IDs, occurrence paths, source captures and original retrieval times are in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w01-shard-coordinator-review-v1/finding-001-concentration-completeness.json`.\n\nPrimary capture SHA-256 bindings:\n- `CS-P-NBRC-1339`: `a731a4c601ae5def7009b9d6600c516810d08a122976fd28a62720ffab122837`.\n- `CS-P-NBRC-881`: `6bf300eade6e04eb3e0047615fbafeb7d8ce795758966df1d562c8462eba2565`.\n- `CS-P-NBRC-1321`: `471a2ea8c7daff318ea0b79a4b7508d5be43f5b823d728d957bdeef3c3ad6e4b`.\n- `CS-P-JCM-1036`: `b50c448cb435eda7dd35bb52c171e56db259c40f097332035990ec931d8ea22d`.\n\nThis is distinct from the previously corrected canary artifact findings in #1159. This reviewer has not performed live issue deduplication or posted an issue.\n\nCoordinator deduplication: current open issues were inspected before filing. #1159 concerns the accepted canary artifacts; #811 and #868 concern other label-index/identity problems. None covers these nine provisional full-shard completeness decisions. This finding belongs to the source-review evidence being prepared for #1160; dependency #1158 remains unchanged.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1163/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167","id":6267763650,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZZ7wg","number":1167,"title":"Keep storage and autoclave atmospheres out of unsupported stock material components","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-08T04:56:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T05:17:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Three unpublished Worker 1 stock proposals turn a storage or autoclaving atmosphere into an asserted material component:\n\n- `CS-PROP-NBRC361_NEUTRALIZED_SULFIDE_STOCK`: Nitrogen is listed as a component based on autoclaving under N2 and sealed storage.\n- `CS-PROP-NBRC1321_SULFIDE_STOCK`: Nitrogen is listed as a component based on storage under N2 after filtration.\n- `KG26-PROP-186-IDENTITY` / `DSMZ863_Sodium_Carbonate_Stock`: Carbon dioxide is listed as a component based on autoclaving sealed vessels under CO2.\n\nThe captured [NBRC361](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=361), [NBRC1321](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1321) and [DSMZ863](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium863.pdf) instructions establish those preparation conditions. They do not specify the gas as a material ingredient or provide a dissolved-gas specification for these stocks. `MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md` section 6 defines `components` as material has-part, not every participant in a preparation procedure.\n\nRetain the atmosphere conditions and exact source provenance in notes/evidence. Remove unsupported gas-component assertions, or supply direct applicable evidence for material inclusion. Recheck component completeness against the source's actual material inputs. Do not invent gas amounts or final dissolved speciation.\n\nKeep the explicit CO2 saturation of the separate bicarbonate preparations distinct: there the source does describe introducing CO2 into the solution, without establishing a numerical concentration. This finding does not remove that sourced distinction or merge any owners.\n\nIndependent finding: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w01-shard-coordinator-review-v2/finding-004-atmosphere-partonomy.json`, SHA256 `34b1123989cef7421dc05cf926f2001c18d0fac12a43463da83eabba8dc48d71`. It binds exact frozen payloads, source captures and case IDs. A coordinator check of the current proposals still found all three gas components. Current issue deduplication and the worker's artifact-finding/issue-plan files showed no existing tracker for this specific defect.\n\nCorrect only proposal artifacts through the guarded writer, preserve earlier versions and obtain independent re-review. No maintained data, scientific hold or release disposition has changed for this finding.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1167/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241","id":6268856056,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdacm-A","number":1241,"title":"Correct Worker02 source scope, quantity prose and review accounting before final acceptance","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:48:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:55:03Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Correct Worker02 source scope, quantity prose and review accounting before final acceptance\n\nReviewed W02 head `0597d00417be4d7cdfb5a31970043eec9bbc88fe`, frozen campaign base `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`. Authoritative peer review is `assembly-v2/review.yaml` (SHA256 `31cac38cae0cfb3dcfae4453a01402dc98d249f70ad9a7698a89b25eed5eae11`) in the sealed W04 independent W02 packet, whose 2,399-member SHA256SUMS is `99306617655b1e3df84368079e49f4341a0fd05667bdf9fedf18dda24f4f7ca7`. The coordinator verified all manifest members, rebound all188 case decisions and106 selected payloads, and independently repeated all106 native guarded writes and baseline/overlay partonomy. Structural validation passes; the scientific verdict remains needs_curation. These are unapplied proposal corrections, not changes already made to main or whole-owner/export approval.\n\nThis tracker groups defects in the same published W02 source/proposal artifact. It does not reopen every historical owner review. Stable finding IDs and complete targets remain in the immutable native review.\n\n| Finding | Exact bounded correction |\n|---|---|\n| W02-F-QUANTITY / W02-RA-02 | Four selected preparation narratives: JCM167 requires water to a final900mL; TOGO M683/JCM665 requires make-up to1L. DSMZ40 C/D/E provider section volumes must not become measured whole-stock aliquots; the inherited DSMZ29 recipe distinguishes water additions and other stocks. MRSsi is expressed per litre, not proven1L of added water. Structured component concentrations were not found defective. Preserve earlier history and append corrections. |\n| W02-F-TYPE / W02C-001 | JCM378 nutrient basal preparation,50%v/v methanol, and0.025%resazurin are marked MINERAL_STOCK, whose schema meaning is concentrated mineral stock. Choose the justified existing category, including OTHER if necessary; no new role inference. |\n| W02-F-METHANOL-SOURCE / W02C-004 | TOGO M1257 is JCM1173-2, using GRMD1173, not1174. Correct the active preferred/mapping/source labels while preserving all six occurrences and the same supported50%v/v stock. |\n| W02-F-MN-SOURCE-CONFLICT / w02-external-b-005 | Case41's17-occurrence manganese applicability includes CM_OCC:9b15f04e391224356807bef1a5f82b76de2fbbcef5ef448cf468b6520d535c3b. The frozen provider entry says MnSO4·xH2O33.8mg/L, but the exact original JCM1503 first trace row says MgCl2·6H2O33.8mg. Partition this source-version/identity conflict from supported Mn occurrences. Nearby source typos do not establish which reagent is right; do not change frozen source bytes or globally assign Mg by guess. |\n| W02-F-FERRIC-AVAILABILITY / w02-external-b-006 | Case124's retained JCM413 and603 captures are successful recipe references to369 and592 with modifications. Correct claims of source unavailability, bind complete modification/base chains and retain genuinely missing reagent/form/quantity facts. Own-CAS and duplicate-owner decisions remain on873. |\n| W02-F-NICKEL-OWNER-BINDING / w02-external-b-008 | Case115 binds only REJECTED Niso4_X_6_H2o. Compare and bind the active Nickel_II_sulfate_hexahydrate owner; preserve the rejected record as history. Do not reactivate it, approve malformedNi2SO4 globally, or erase the historical EXCLUDED_REJECTED review. |\n| W02-F-EVIDENCE-CLASSIFICATION / W02-RA-01, w02-external-b-007, W02C-COVERAGE-001 | Nine actual Nothing-found responses are not positive recipe evidence: three are referenced by active cases2/30/152/184, JCM1250 also remains in the ferric proposal, five are historical unlinked evidence. Distinguish the failed CAS Common Chemistry detail response too. b2-chebi-30729 is valid ontology evidence, not original ammonium-reagent recipe evidence. Preserve original bytes/times; successful bacmedia recoveries are separate sources, not retrospective success. |\n| W02-F-PUBLICATION-LINEAGE / W02-ASSEMBLY-01 | Add an immutable author-published ledger covering all72 prior stable finding IDs and735 historical finding/reference objects, linking complete targets, exact old hashes, deduplicated issues, corrections, independent re-reviews and residual holds. A private external ledger or broad handoff link does not provide this author publication lineage. Do not blanket reopen/close corrected science. |\n\nPrimary checks: [JCM167](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=167); [TOGO M683](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M683); [TOGO M2491](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2491); [TOGO M1257](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M1257); [JCM1503](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1503). The sealed exact captures and coordinator primary-finding-readback.json retain response hashes and original access times. JCM1503 SHA256 is `01c7a36ad95a0d476f5fc1806413145c63c56de7bf270d6fbdd006795c6800ef`.\n\n| Proposal | Owner | Exact selected SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a-proposal-chrome-alum` | `data/ingredients/mapped/CrKSO42_X_12_H2O.yaml` | `e4f2fb4d6d39e19bdbad76bbd5a8cedbf960507fb825714922fb6a4d0d19c5d0` |\n| `a-proposal-strontium-sulfate` | `data/ingredients/mapped/Strontium_sulfate.yaml` | `ce0a68da191d5d3b0aa447b83d1d6aacb11594d7528e48f3210c39804c9fcfae` |\n| `a2-proposal-dsmz40-cde-mixed-preparation` | `data/ingredients/mapped/dsmz40_cde_mixed_preparation.yaml` | `1d4bb6decf8b68edebbdc1dabf670804624c20d01b0e59adb5bd0526d25cd97e` |\n| `a2-proposal-jcm167-precarbonate-basal-agar` | `data/ingredients/mapped/jcm167_precarbonate_basal_agar.yaml` | `4409f51db458621b0cb67ef34639fee49863bbf90e9ea8fd97ebda74267ebd5c` |\n| `a2-proposal-jcm378-preaddition-basal-preparation` | `data/ingredients/mapped/jcm378_preaddition_basal_preparation.yaml` | `6511f1be0d51490e09fb693ff8354d18a26c08d6eeccb7e7192dac894eb49844` |\n| `a2-proposal-jcm665-preaddition-iron-gel-base` | `data/ingredients/mapped/jcm665_preaddition_iron_gel_base.yaml` | `db1b027dde687f0afabdb0068f6aa0bce7006eb5f5206597581595ed92b96fb4` |\n| `a2-proposal-manganese-sulfate-variable-hydrate` | `data/ingredients/mapped/manganese_sulfate_variable_hydrate.yaml` | `ac7c4e146dd7b40fc76b77066c6e36e63e52394adaf98f81e4d1c8534bc838a3` |\n| `a2-proposal-togo-m2491-mrssi-base` | `data/ingredients/mapped/togo_m2491_mrssi_base.yaml` | `3838ea36856afdd637869e7818a855779a60d63067406ba08ede81bc80f045c4` |\n| `b2-proposal-Ferric_ammonium_EDTA` | `data/ingredients/mapped/Ferric_ammonium_EDTA.yaml` | `a34676d09ff73c29cbd8d6dd8db3d80723c459bbc392a747962c2651ad71abf5` |\n| `b2-proposal-methanol_50_percent_vv_jcm_sources` | `data/ingredients/mapped/methanol_50_percent_vv_jcm_sources.yaml` | `1e7ef83bf7afacdc950c4e2013a6ce1dc3550e503a1810780ebdd50ca27b0348` |\n| `b2-proposal-resazurin_0025_percent_atcc_chopped_meat` | `data/ingredients/mapped/resazurin_0025_percent_atcc_chopped_meat.yaml` | `43559067e33088d4353e4b9d37babf9996f6304afbcedbba1b15d0b77069d45a` |\n| `w02-v2-ferric-variable-composed` | `data/ingredients/mapped/Fe2_So43_X_N_H2o.yaml` | `ca1c64bdf0ab2178eb19f91ab46103783b39343787f5bdd151cb28f12b3fe20c` |\n\nDeduplication:1201 covers missing feasible curation, not these incorrect active quantity/category/source and publication fields.1173 and1223 track other workers' publication lineage.873 owns ferric identity/alias competition and receives the exact companion comment. Live all-state source/name and comment searches found no exact dedicated W02 tracker for this set; this does not assert that every historical GitHub comment is indexed.\n\nPreserve published original payloads/reviews, capture timestamps, histories, rejected text and all precise source/form/role/release holds. Prepare immutable corrected proposals through existing guarded validation, record claim-specific changes, and obtain independent review of the exact successor. No corpus application, owner merge, gate/schema/test/producer change or approval transfer follows from this issue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1241/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193","id":6268001338,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZocOg","number":1193,"title":"Complete source-defined worker05 formulation curation before final shard acceptance","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2026-11-08T05:34:32Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T10:44:19Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Worker05's published source-review head `b44430c9230e62f9d9d73154484311b77442e73e` declares the shard complete, but at least one no-change disposition defers curation that the campaign already authorizes rather than documenting an unavailable scientific prerequisite.\n\nAffected case: `KG_CASE:b58f2778ba8c8905faf5cddf634ff4d5059978baa1b2489af2eb4db7f7e9fef1`, MediaDive ingredient1382, Grace's Insect Medium. Existing source owner: `data/ingredients/unmapped/Graces_Insect_Medium.yaml`, SHA256 `98d818debe40f93d28b7c08b2a7437b6a3c8566e12c857aa7f42fd3c1cdafa3e`.\n\nThe [committed decision](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/b44430c9230e62f9d9d73154484311b77442e73e/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-05/media/decisions.json) explicitly binds the source to Sigma G8142 and cites the manufacturer's complete formula. Its no-change and missing-requirement fields say to curate that formula and review component identities. There is no proposal, and no distinct missing evidence for the whole supplied product is identified.\n\nThe [manufacturer formula](https://www.sigmaaldrich.cn/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/product/documents/172/423/g8142for.pdf) distinguishes G8142 liquid1x from G9771 powder, including bicarbonate treatment. Worker evidence `MEDIA-SIGMA-G8142-FORMULA` retains the PDF at SHA256 `7a07a208abd686522d82c3d61bc682af4e377ebd226bdbe786c2f9e84727b140`. This is a lead for supplied-product curation, not approval of any generic medium equivalence or every component identity.\n\nMAPPING_SEMANTICS sections3 and6 and the add-media workflow distinguish whole preparation identity from component grounding. Named ungrounded parts may remain explicit; a missing component CURIE is not by itself proof that an evidence-defined preparation must stay entirely uncurated. The campaign requires justified curation, not only a list of future curation tasks.\n\nPlease reassess this case and the other worker05 no-change dispositions whose stated blocker is simply to curate, define or reconcile an already identified formulation. For each, either prepare a concrete evidence-backed proposal through the existing proposal workflow, or record the exact unresolved scientific fact and the primary-source searches actually attempted. Preserve historical/source scope, competing-owner boundaries, raw labels, prior holds, and separate full-payload/release review. Do not invent a catalog variant, infer a complete formula from a source name, merge owners, treat all product names as resolved, or approve roles.\n\nFor G8142 specifically, verify the source-to-product attribution and all current owner occurrences before choosing whether the existing owner can be specialized or a separate source-qualified preparation is needed. Transcribe only supported formulation claims; preserve any uncertainty in individual component form or quantity explicitly. Independent re-review must cover the revised disposition/proposal and final head.\n\nDeduplication: the complete652-visible-issue all-state snapshot and relevant Grace/G8142/worker05 title/body matches contained no exact completeness finding. #1176 and #1177 cover separate peptone/Sea Salts defects. This issue does not reopen those or supersede a scientific hold.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239","id":6268746435,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdaV6ww","number":1239,"title":"Retire the FerriSeltz formulation alias from generic ferric ammonium citrate","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:32:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T07:32:24Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Independent follow-up to the preserved W07 two-owner review, manifest SHA256 `fa86b7a9bdc84ae7e796d2dcb507d2dd031a0f8c1462492a45bff2fdfb00c04c`. I rehashed all2,339 manifest-listed files, rebound both reviewed candidates to the active37-candidate set, inspected the exact primary sections and reproduced native synonym/row behavior. These are unapplied candidates. Original reviews, histories and genuine scope holds remain; neither review nor this triage approves release.\n\n**FAC-F01** confirms an inherited whole-product/active-ingredient conflation. The authentic `data/ingredients/mapped/Ferric_Ammonium_Citrate.yaml` beforeimage SHA256 `ae646b9c5f3e9c8ec01d939e1b97733259825a14e4a8a03626bc65453035426e` and current reconciled candidate `70f3b34f5cddc485f53242cd6f04ff1bc9fd6598e2be906f6da89393af8f2234` both retain:\n\n`FerriSeltz` — `EXACT_SYNONYM`, source `kg_microbe`, at `synonyms[7]`.\n\nBoth native MIM synonym policy and pinned Claw76c1 publishability classify it as resolving. The [official PMDA FerriSeltz powder20% label](https://www.pmda.go.jp/PmdaSearch/iyakuDetail/ResultDataSetPDF/180078_7290004B1030_1_09), September2024 revision, page1 §3.1, instead specifies600mg ferric ammonium citrate in a3g product with flavour, aspartame, sodium bicarbonate and tartaric acid. Page2 §19 describes the active ingredient. Exact PDF SHA256 `ed32d4c1c55534ae3ebf4eb7e51739d645b751fb63dfe51126c49fc29cb4a98d`; the independent reviewer inspected the full text and the composition-table image. The formulated product is not identical to its generic FAC component. No medium occurrence is inferred to use this medicine.\n\nRetain the exact label and source as provenance-only `REJECTED_LABEL`, with claim-specific evidence and a truthful curation event. Preserve the supported generic CHEBI31604 material identity, all three new medium aliases and their eight assigned occurrences, raw histories and source-specific uncertainty. Do not invent a fixed molecular formula/stoichiometry, green/brown grade, supplier, nitrogen role, new medicine owner or source reassignment. If the formulation is ever separately requested, it needs its own supported identity/composition scope.\n\n**FAC-F02 qualification:** four Role/Properties sentences at synonyms[0–3] are already nonresolving in both native policies. Optional provenance-preserving REJECTED_LABEL typing can accompany curation, but this is not an export leak, independent acceptance blocker or evidence that the underlying role is false. Keep the provisional nitrogen-role assessment separate.\n\nSource review: `20261108T071449Z-worker07-fac-independent`, native YAML SHA256 `cf1d6a381fe37bac2031e2d45c1b57c8c9190bfd58ec5c42dbfb1296520c282a`. Exact triage and native controls: `C/preflight/fac-polypeptone-findings-triage-v1/`. Fresh all-state GitHub searches including title/body/comments for FerriSeltz returned zero results; broader FAC-name searches returned #1201 and historical #213, neither the exact product-alias finding. This issue describes the frozen authentic before/current private candidate, not an unverified statement about live main.\n\nCorrected whole-candidate bytes need independent review and native alias checks before source application. Preserve mapping/source/role/export holds and all historical evidence. No new schema, gate, threshold or owner-selection change is needed.\n\n<!-- mim-fingerprints:ferric-ammonium-citrate-ferriseltz-product-exact-alias -->\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1239/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173","id":6267902825,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdZibaQ","number":1173,"title":"Track Worker 1 full-shard findings separately from the canary provenance","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-11-08T05:18:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T05:37:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Worker 1's full-shard evidence at `1894d28d94df4e654ebce9752c23a2321aeb21c5` assigns `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-1` through `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-12` to #1159 in `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-01/shard/independent_review/final-188-scientific-review-v1.json`. Its active shard report repeats that attribution. The live #1159 body covers only the three earlier canary findings (`IR-DRAFT-1`, `IR-DRAFT-2`, `IR-VALIDATION-1`) and has no comments expanding its scope.\n\nThis issue records the distinct full-shard finding set and the publication provenance correction `W01-PUBLISHED-001`. Preserve #1159's canary identity. The full-shard review reports these corrections in isolated proposals, independently re-reviewed before publication:\n\n| Finding | Defect and corrected scope |\n| --- | --- |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-1 | Distinguish the unsuccessful JCM956 retrieval from the explicit JCM574 fallback and actual MDS context. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-2 | Remove the false discrepancy between frozen `10 MILLIMOLAR` and `10 mM` for case105; retain the actual reagent-form uncertainty. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-3 | Correct named case104's receiving dose from 1 to 2 mL. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-4 | Distinguish case138's current recipe1188 direct reference to852 from the frozen1187 inheritance narrative. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-5 | Correct case103's receiving dose from 5 to10 mL. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-6 | Correct case112's receiving dose from 1 to1.5 mL. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-7 | Remove root40's unsupported aqueous assertion; retain the actual solvent evidence gap. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-8 | Keep Middlebrook7H10 dry base distinct from the NCIT enriched finished medium. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-9 | Retire source-local/generic aliases that would resolve globally, including bare numbered pointers; qualify the JCM431 stock name and mapping label. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-10 | Reconcile four duplicate proposal families while preserving each source-case/occurrence lineage. The NBRC1257/1321 bicarbonate and sulfide pairs are also tracked by #1166; NBRC1339 phenanthrene and NBRC943 Metal44 are the other two families. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-11 | Preserve added-water quantities without treating them as final solution volumes or inferred final concentrations; retain explicit preparation and comparison bases. |\n| IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT-12 | Correct false or unrelated missing-evidence requirements for cases38/64 and34/59/66, preserving the source-supported remaining gaps. |\n\nThe separate coordinator findings remain on #1163, #1164, #1166, #1167 and #1168. This tracker does not replace them or grant maintained-record, mapping, role, component or release approval.\n\nAppend an immutable provenance correction or successor, update active report/issue references and the PR description, and preserve old primary captures, proposal payloads, native saved reviews and canary files byte-for-byte. Do not rewrite the historical review merely to conceal its mistaken issue reference. The published correction must bind the exact prior review hash and all twelve finding IDs. Obtain independent final-head re-review of the new references and confirm the scientific payloads are unchanged.\n\nIndependent evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/w01-published-head-review-v1/finding-001-tracker-scope.json`; prior full-shard review SHA256 `02b2be72b448d35b573ad992a3d2c98afcd3f16430709e10d6837564b595edcf`; active report SHA256 `762ba8d961cfdfc856c724d2a4b232cc776bbc43861e34a0f7d28af70b06f1df`. A live all-state GitHub issue search for `IR-SHARD-ARTIFACT` found no existing dedicated tracker. The local evidence search included ignored files. No scientific payload defect was found in the independent 188-case/76-proposal reassessment.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1173/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223","id":6268390887,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdaAN5w","number":1223,"title":"Preserve Worker07 resolved review findings in an immutable issue-linked ledger","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T06:36:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T06:36:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Preserve Worker07’s resolved review findings in an immutable issue-linked ledger\n\nThe published Worker07 head `fbfa032435ea1c399ae9b98bfedadb9ed639430d` contains 18 resolved internal findings across four independent receipts. Its handoff only identifies three newly filed source/owner issues (MIM #1169, #1170 and CultureMech #672), plus older owner issues. The internal remediation lineage is not explicitly bound to a deduplicated issue/disposition ledger. This is the same kind of publication-accounting gap addressed for Worker01 in #1173; it does not undo the scientific corrections.\n\n| Original finding | Scope | Immutable review |\n|---|---|---|\n| C-A-01 | Approximate KOH7.3g omitted from stock payloads though explicit in bothprimaryrecipes. Preserve approximate amount in notes, not as exact finalconcentration. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/c-review-a-final.json` (`8fde04550a6a`) |\n| C-A-02 | PARTIAL enum misused for unresolved chemicalIDs or unreported fullstock. COMPLETE means complete sourceconstituentlist; PARTIAL means explicitlyomitted additionalcomponents; UNKNOWN meanssource doesnot establishcompleteness. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/c-review-a-final.json` (`8fde04550a6a`) |\n| C-A-03 | Explicit independent conventionalnomenclature evidence needed for sodiumcitratedihydrate→trisodium before exactaliasaddition; no vendorassignment tosource. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/c-review-a-final.json` (`8fde04550a6a`) |\n| C-A-04 | Documentprimarypursuit and source-specific missingrequirements for all four sodiumborate sourcefamilies, notonly failedMediaDB288. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/c-review-a-final.json` (`8fde04550a6a`) |\n| C-A-05 | Recovered TOGO annotation is Sodium carbonate, not bicarbonate; author corrected this factual misstatement without changing ambiguity hold. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/c-review-a-final.json` (`8fde04550a6a`) |\n| A-REVIEW-B-91 | Frozen complete UTEX DAS recipe composition[3].evidence explicitly names Sigma V6629. Draft class-only rationale overlooks this exact supplier identity lead. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/a-review-b-final.json` (`0f2b8233ce28`) |\n| A-REVIEW-B-90 | Seven MediaDB sodium EDTA occurrences have only ontology evidence referenced; source-specific original references are present in frozen recipes and must be pursued independently. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/a-review-b-final.json` (`0f2b8233ce28`) |\n| A-REVIEW-B-116 | Seventeen sodium ammonium phosphate contexts link only one article DOI; confirm family applicability and pursue other distinct reference families from frozen recipes. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/a-review-b-final.json` (`0f2b8233ce28`) |\n| A-REVIEW-B-EVIDENCE-KINDS | Captured MediaDive /rest/compound/1118,291,2154,1732 return JSON status400 WrongCall; JCM665/688 return Nothing found. These were marked primary_source although they establish only access/source-availability limits. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/a-review-b-final.json` (`0f2b8233ce28`) |\n| A-REVIEW-B-STOCK-SCOPE | New JCM706 nominal-stock payload says0.05mL per10mL receiving medium; original JCM706 specifies per4.7mL. JCM1422 current primary4mL differs from frozen10mL. Inheritance text1463/1462 andM708/687 is copied across95/121/134 without per-case relevance. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/a-review-b-final.json` (`0f2b8233ce28`) |\n| B-C-01 | DSM1053 current source does not repeat ferric hydrate; correct source attribution. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/b-independent-c-review-final.json` (`5dac5bf702ef`) |\n| B-C-02 | PARTIAL completeness incorrectly justified by unresolved identities/solvent: use schema list completeness semantics. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/b-independent-c-review-final.json` (`5dac5bf702ef`) |\n| B-C-03 | RESTingredient response does not carry occurrence stock attributes; source locator must bind frozen source_record or matched original recipe. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/b-independent-c-review-final.json` (`5dac5bf702ef`) |\n| B-C-04 | Explicit nominal stock context permits bounded proposal; remaining percentage/solvent details need not defer source identity. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/parts/b-independent-c-review-final.json` (`5dac5bf702ef`) |\n| INTEGRATION-01 | Verified same nine-input JCM900/JCM979 stock consolidated once, retaining both primary provenance sets, malformed molybdate string and approximate KOH quantity. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/integration-review-final.json` (`fef705ca9f1d`) |\n| INTEGRATION-02 | Validation receipt separately labels 2956 catalogue records and 2862 unique identifiers; prior mislabeled preliminary receipt retained. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/integration-review-final.json` (`fef705ca9f1d`) |\n| INTEGRATION-03 | Four concrete source-qualified nominal stocks and explicitly guarded decision deltas independently reviewed; missing form/solvent/percent details remain UNKNOWN. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/integration-review-final.json` (`fef705ca9f1d`) |\n| INTEGRATION-04 | Successor native wrapper records fifth confirmed Sodium_Malate DL-alias conflict while retaining source salt-stoichiometry uncertainty; initial review/finding preserved. | `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-07/captures/integration-review-final.json` (`fef705ca9f1d`) |\n\nPlease preserve all original reviews and payloads. Add a successor ledger linking every item to its issue, correction and exact independent re-review, with the prior artifact hashes. Reference that ledger from the active handoff. The scientific successor should retain the current 188-case/100-proposal content and the 17-occurrence #1203 correction. No owner application or approval follows.\n\nDeduplication: the independent reviewer read all committed Worker07 report and native review additions, including their gitignored ancestor directories, and live #1169/#1170 bodies/comments. The coordinator verified the 18 review references against the exact published Git blobs, checked 679 current open and closed issue bodies, and searched the exact finding IDs. No existing issue covering this lineage gap was found in those checks.\n\nKnown source/owner issues and coordinator reconciliation requirements, including1203 and1210, remain separate.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1223/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6268732544,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABdaVEgA","number":1237,"title":"Reconcile source-bound preparation families before installing duplicate or unsupported owners","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":23,"created_at":"2026-11-08T07:30:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T11:53:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The completed independent preparation-comparison packets identify duplicate proposed preparations, source-continuity conflicts and unsupported claims of disjointness. This issue tracks only the bounded family decisions below. These are isolated proposals; no record merge, new namespace, scientific approval or export release is authorized by the review.\n\nAll three sealed packets were independently hash-checked: Worker01 878 files, Worker05 390, Worker10 526, with no hash mismatch or unlisted file in the ignored-inclusive inventories. Their assignments partition the 67 mechanical family leads (26/22/19); this means comparison coverage, not 67 resolved or approved identities. The exact 28 retained finding/obligation IDs are reduced to 26 rows in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/family-findings-triage-v1/findings-matrix-v2.json`. Original authors, skeptical reviews, proposal bytes, primary capture times/hashes, source cases and occurrences remain immutable.\n\nA source accession, filename, receiving dose, missing carrier, unknown pH or unspecified hydrate does not prove a distinct supplied preparation. Nor does it prove equality. Source-qualified partial proposals remain useful; overlapping candidates need a defined scope or the missing evidence before simultaneous installation. No unknown is filled by guessing. Source-batch water and final-volume instructions remain separate, and immediate-list completeness is independent of molecular grounding.\n\n| Findings / frozen entries | Sourced conclusion and bounded next action |\n|---|---|\n| W01-FPC-PA-001 + MIN-F03; 573/810, maintained ATCC_Wolfes_Vitamin_Mix | JCM197, NBRC837 and NBRC903 give the same ten nominal vitamins and amounts plus1L water. Prepare one combined nominal candidate preserving all source-specific processing. The maintained ATCC owner has authentic branded MD-VS history and a D-(+) calcium-pantothenate specification; JCM/NBRC only say calcium pantothenate. Preserve that distinction in what the evidence asserts: unspecified stereo proves neither sameness nor difference. Do not automatically reuse ATCC or install two source-number owners. Establish the applicability bridge or explicitly decide nominal-recipe versus supplied-product scope before co-installation. |\n| MIN-F01; 624/657 | DSM590/1144 Hutner tables and preparation match at nominal scope. Preserve CaCl2·2H2O3.335g versus3.34g rounding and both malformed molybdate strings as literal unresolved assertions; do not turn a typographical discrepancy into a different chemical. Prepare one source-union nominal recipe candidate. Both underlying Metals44 instructions are retained; the current automatically extracted portal is not a historical erratum. |\n| MIN-F02, W05-CR-F02; 381–384/624/657/705 | Wolfe JCM470/DSM792, modified Wolfe ATCC1190/1191 versus JCM221, and Hutner JCM900/979 comparisons have explicit unresolved hydrate/reagent or preparation details. Correct claims that missing qualifiers prove incompatibility. Do not infer JCM470's variable Mn hydrate as monohydrate, or transfer ATCC final-volume/form-specific instructions to JCM221. Preserve the positively different JCM149 MgSO4 quantity14.45g versus29.7g. |\n| W01-FPC-PA-003; 747 plus existing JCM403 B12 owner | NBRC1321 explicitly gives cyanocobalamin5mg with100ml water; JCM403 specifies generic B12 at matching nominal quantities. Preserve both levels of specificity. Missing JCM vitamer/preparation evidence is an unresolved relation, not a proved difference or an exact identity bridge. Coordinate the existing JCM403 promotion/pointer correction under1201/1227; do not create a competing owner by accession alone. |\n| W01-PREP-B-001; 619 | NBRC1507 names0.1M Tris/HCl pH7.5 stock but does not list free hydrochloric acid as a separate component. Remove that unsupported free-acid has-part claim. Preserve the literal named buffer, strength and pH with unknown complete composition; do not substitute dry Tris-HCl salt or invent solvent/neutralization. |\n| W01-PREP-B-002 + CHEM-COMP-003; 669 | JCM1479 positively specifies a5% L-cysteine-HCl-monohydrate stock atpH7. Unreported pH of other5% stocks does not establish a different substance. Correct the comparison wording, retain stock/solid separation and the unknown percentage basis/carrier/titrant. |\n| CHEM-COMP-002; 6/13 | NBRC1020 prints Na2WO4; JCM317 explicitly prints dihydrate, both at4mg with4mg selenite and1L water. Remove the claim that omission proves anhydrous NBRC1020 or disjointness. Preserve both literal tables and ask only for the missing supplied form if full chemical equivalence is needed. |\n| CHEM-COMP-004; 943/944/946/106 | Literal35%,32%,25% HCl and qualitative concentrated labels have unknown comparable bases; M2305/M2746 even call their25% input concentrated. Correct categorical disjointness without converting percentages or inventing a carrier. Retain source qualification; an explicit common partial-material scope or comparable formulation evidence is needed before consolidation. |\n| BIO-COMP-005; 328/333 with283/287/288/290 | Historical MJ and JCM1216 0.1x artificial-seawater formulations remain partly unspecified. Missing recipe/version is not evidence of a different formulation. Preserve the source-qualified preparations, positive known differences and exact missing historical MJ/1x-base specification; no guessed formula or wholesale seawater merge. |\n| BIO-COMP-001; 201/476 | CM0643 prepared broth and dry powder are different supplied forms. The source handles for entry201 use1000ml/10ml broth; entry476 weighs33g powder. Correct entry201's dry-powder representation and account for its authentic existing broth provenance. Retain powder separate from prepared broth, water and receiving supplements; the same catalogue does not erase the supplied-form boundary. MICRO:0002186 describes liquid, so any use requires whole-broth§3 scope review and must not identify powder. |\n| BIO-F02; 971 + Swine_Serum | The new DSM1076b heat-inactivated swine-serum proposal uses MediaDive960, already the creation source of Swine_Serum/UNMAPPED_0536. Reconcile or promote through that authentic preimage/history. Do not add a second same-source owner or label the separate generic Porcine_Serum/MD967 untreated. Heat schedule remains unknown. |\n| BIO-F03; 970 + Bovine_Calf_Serum | JCM1303 heat-inactivated calf serum uses MediaDive2061, already the import source of Bovine_Calf_Serum. Audit its broader/Gibco occurrences and partition their applicability before narrowing or adding an owner. Missing historical heat metadata is not an untreated claim. No wholesale repurposing or maintained-owner merge. |\n| BIO-F04; 893/908/914/916/922 | Withdraw unsupported serum exclusions: bovine does not exclude fetal; gamma irradiation does not exclude heat treatment; unspecified heat schedule need not differ from a specified one. Retain positive age/species/catalogue/process facts and actual30/45/60minute or active/inactivated differences. No forced product equivalence. |\n| BIO-F05; 904/906 | JCM946 supports56C30min heating and filtration before addition, but not their relative order. Clarify only that ordering claim. DSM1021 explicitly requires sterile fetal/newborn alternatives; preserve sterility for the selected newborn scope without inventing heat or filter treatment. |\n| BIO-F06; 300/921 | Oxoid CM0331 and TOGO M2224 disclose the same nominal dry base: special peptone23g, starch1g, NaCl5g, agar10g, pH7.3±0.2. Prepare one combined formulation candidate while retaining which source actually states the catalogue. Before installation, account for existing Columbia_Blood_Agar_Base's mixed Oxoid/Difco provenance; do not repurpose the entire owner. Preserve the distinct Difco/BBL/EH formulations. Blood and reconstitution water are not dry-base parts. |\n| BIO-F07; 980 | Replace a search-wrapper-as-primary assertion with the recovered2009 BD manufacturer manual capture, p158. Keep original wrapper, older manual edition and failed URLs as historical evidence. This verifies the nominal Difco formulation, not a historical lot or arbitrary vendor equivalence. |\n| BIO-F08; 919 | Current ATCC0988 is explicitly reformulated asMD2611 and specifies ATCC30-2020 plus55C treatment; frozen TOGO M2578 preserves older fetal/newborn alternatives and unknown schedule. Keep both versions and their exact applicability. Same URL is not same document; this is a version obligation, not a finding that the frozen transcription is false. |\n| CHEM-COMP-006; 35/36 | Reassess new claim-specific resolver dispositions. The fully specified0.01M FeSO4·7H2O in0.02N HCl name is not shown to be a non-name merely because a global alias was undesirable. Bicarbonate footnote pointers have different ambiguity. Preserve all existing rejected entries; do not blanket-reactivate or blanket-reject authentic labels. Under§3, any new rejection needs claim-specific evidence; owned-name suppression applies only when its ownership condition holds. Historical1173 lineage is not a new scientific decision. |\n\nAdditional reconciliation groups with positive evidence can proceed to isolated candidate preparation, with exact-byte independent review before application:\n\n- DAIGO395-01681 entries188/474: one named dry product, eight manufacturer components. Preserve the manufacturer/JCM peptone wording and exact hydrate, the3.15g listed sum versus3.2g preparation instruction, and both histories. Do not invent another constituent, agar, water, generic DSM1537 applicability or wholesale KG1402 routing. The local identifier is already shared; choose one readable destination by the product scope, not author order.\n- Mixed phosphate entries873/940: one nominal preparation from equal volumes of1M KH2PO4 and1M Na2HPO4. Preserve50+50ml versus10+10ml batches and PBBM-onlypH7.2. The immediate input list can be complete without claiming its input stocks' exact hydrate, solvent or neutralization chemistry.\n- HEPES-KOH1M entries449/450 (W05-CR-F01): both sources positively name the same nominal strength/neutralizer; receiving-mediumpH7.14/9.0 is not stockpH. Recommend an explicit common bounded nominal scope if that is the intended owner model; otherwise retain candidate holds for actual stockpH/carrier/neutralization evidence. Do not install two proved-distinct preparations based solely on source numbers.\n- 95% ethanol entries460–463 (W05-CR-F03): preserve proven within-protocol reuse and every occurrence. A shared bounded partial-material scope is an option, but neither four distinct complete formulations nor equality follows without percentage basis/carrier/denaturant/product evidence. Do not infer95%v/v aqueous NCIT identity. Missing composition is not permission to discard the supported partial material.\n\nExisting trackers are reused, not duplicated:1206 JCM852;1210 sodium-thiosulfate tetrahydrate;1202 Polypeptone;1212 Phytone/SoyPeptone;1217 W06 source/solvent provenance;1221 EBIOS;1204 rumen. For rumen the current sourced decision explicitly leaves the three dependent parents' literal rumen-fluid components UNMAPPED; the older comparison suggestion to redirect them to clarified fluid is superseded, not fresh evidence. The Tris-HCl parent-grade defect is filed separately because its exact record correction/native repro is distinct from these formulation decisions.\n\nPrimary source anchors: [JCM197](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197), [NBRC903](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=903), [ATCC2672](https://www.atcc.org/-/media/product-assets/documents/microbial-media-formulations/2/6/7/2/atcc-medium-2672.pdf?rev=7f27672230474579b9151e4c2ec9f20a), [DSM590](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium590.pdf), [DSM1144](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1144.pdf), [JCM470](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=470), [NBRC1507](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1507), [DSM1076b](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1076b.pdf), [JCM1303](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1303), [Oxoid CM0331 specification](https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MBD/Specification-Sheets/PS-CM0331-V6.pdf), [TOGO M2224](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2224), [BD2009 manual](https://fsl.nmsu.edu/documents/difcobblmanual_2nded_lowres.pdf), [DAIGO manufacturer](https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/jp/product/detail/W01N0139-0168.html). Every capture's exact original URL/time/hash and case binding is retained in the triage indexes and source packets; links alone are not treated as immutable evidence.\n\nDo not apply the original frozen W06 payloads just because their historical paths still exist. Six selected W06 payloads and its new EBIOS proposal have advanced and need exact successor comparisons. W07's observed successor was metadata-only in the source comparison, but its actual selected bytes still require final intake readback. All source, role and release holds remain content-bound.\n\nExact frozen source origins retained for these findings (later successors require explicit bridges):\n\n| Entry | Original proposal | Source head | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6 | `w01::NSV4-PROP-NBRC_1020_Se_W_Solution` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `235072e64c69a7dc51f9386f0664d69ffab234a5a0cca427cf4b4b18b37de0e7` |\n| 13 | `w01::NSV4-PROP-JCM_317_Se_W_Solution` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `1603001c438fc6e321f1f105cff5ebd5a9f2be169e5657493de1d8b49a4ace62` |\n| 35 | `w01::CS-PROP-JCM1430_FERROUS_SULFATE_HCL_STOCK` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `6e0ae3d8ec0984d7e29034b2fd41d3589f26fb7f236bdcc7a829d632837e0c59` |\n| 36 | `w01::CS-PROP-NBRC1321_CO2_BICARBONATE_STOCK` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `61c0a226a8a99d96b43657f6e00075e901ce051a698b01bd99f6ab6f1d88717c` |\n| 106 | `w02::a2-proposal-togo-m2746-m2305-hydrochloric-acid-25percent` | `0597d00417be4d7cdfb5a31970043eec9bbc88fe` | `70c016d0e74a8487668258f66ab8ae63722e4ecbf6cce3b4c7890caaa9054a51` |\n| 188 | `w03::b-proposal-daigo-r2a` | `1196d5bc3aaba7563b829d5cbe7e54722fccc35d` | `5603b8878ca3460906dcc26b33c29db602661773eb3a598ad293ae7cd525b22f` |\n| 201 | `w03::b-proposal-cm0643` | `1196d5bc3aaba7563b829d5cbe7e54722fccc35d` | `1646156e0153d035e585214dd25eaa6275a423bc41920aa34cc68a02992aa4e6` |\n| 283 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_492_modified_mj_synthetic_seawater` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `ddd35feefd2df9b1f2a3d721f5b3d89926988efc6e7210a1269e243d324d8f16` |\n| 287 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_651_artificial_seawater_05x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `0adde845da6ee89a25d28a821e889727dd5136c6ae3015c4e6eb17781dc9095a` |\n| 288 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_910_artificial_seawater_1x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `4557113d7ff49fdd8722ba409e1d5e1016d44b5f51f528a644c0048d9eeaa107` |\n| 290 | `w04::BIO-PROPOSAL-jcm_1269_artificial_seawater_4x` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `71008fd600cde88d17a6315c0147b00ca48890df2cb53ce643c794853640899c` |\n| 300 | `w04::media-followup-oxoid_cm0331_columbia_blood_agar_base` | `548e7bdd0ce2a68b3ae0df6ad7a6150a4e5c9bb9` | `560e2e3301550c952b729956e1a04c87941304888130adbe52a254e747207e