rum1303` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `c5095e48aa60fc9dde875bc49e1d1628f9869ab53d606ca10c42622de9b77a78` |\n| 971 | `w10::sv1-kg-swine-serum1076b` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `855514ece2c881918f44112a0f3c52cb855b0e05642cf5af267235a1936a10c7` |\n| 980 | `w10::sv1-kg-difco-columbia1270` | `468766d941e35a74eb2de3c95096660987277d9b` | `07b3aa3689dbee44e18c5c4d416ebee0ba5920a5eb044cd7901cda9d7f8ab0e7` |\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288","id":5085142057,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABLxkcKQ","number":288,"title":"35 zero-occurrence STOCK_SOLUTION records left unminted — decide whether the population should be finished","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-08-06T22:27:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T03:26:09Z","closed_at":"2026-08-07T03:26:09Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found finishing #114's non-chemical disposition.\n\nThe UNMAPPED residual contained **96 records typed `STOCK_SOLUTION`** — named multi-component lab preparations (`Wolfe's vitamin mix`, `Wolfe's mineral mix`, trace-metal and amino-acid mixes). None has an ontology term and none could: a preparation is not a substance. Searching CHEBI, NCIT, MeSH, FOODON and ENVO by label and synonym returned a hit for **2 of 96, and both were false** — `PBS` → `NCIT:C122728` *'TSPO wt Allele'* (a gene allele) and `Trace minerals` → an M-prefixed MeSH concept id rather than a D/C descriptor.\n\nI minted `kgmicrobe.ingredient:` identifiers for the **61 that occur in at least one medium**, following the convention 12 existing mapped `STOCK_SOLUTION` records already use (`FALLBACK_REGISTRY`, no parent — a multi-component mix does not narrow to a single compound).\n\n**I deliberately left the other 35**, which have `total_occurrences: 0`. The reasoning was that an identifier for a preparation nothing uses is not worth the published row.\n\nThat is a judgement, not an obvious call, and it leaves the population half-done. Worth deciding explicitly:\n\n- **Finish them** — consistency, and a zero-occurrence record today may be used tomorrow; the marginal cost is 35 rows.\n- **Leave them** — the SSSOM stays proportional to what is actually used, and zero-occurrence records are the ones most likely to be import noise or duplicates that should be merged rather than minted.\n- **Triage first** — check whether any of the 35 are spelling variants of the 61 already minted (e.g. `Mc_general_salts` vs `Mc_general_salts_SO4free` are genuinely different, but others may not be). That would make some of them merges rather than mints, which is a better outcome than either option above.\n\nI would lean on the third: the zero-occurrence tail is exactly where duplicate/variant labels accumulate, and minting them would fix that population in place rather than deduplicating it.\n\nRelated: #114, #218 (duplicate identifiers), #226.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/288/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}